    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Change\n\nAdded a 3-line guard to `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n```java\nCollection<Owner> owners = this.clinicService.findAllOwners();\nif (CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n}\n```\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:**\n- **One file, one method touched** \u2014 the whole cost is multiplied by files touched, so I avoided creating new files or editing other methods.\n- **Reused the existing `CityCodes.count` helper** (which already counts owners in a candidate's city, case-insensitively, for the customer-code logic) instead of adding new logic. That means no new class and no growth of a complex unit \u2014 just a single early-return branch, keeping `changed_lines` and the added complexity minimal.\n\nThe check returns **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners, satisfying the spec and the `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` acceptance test (fills a city to 50, expects the 51st to be rejected).",
